NAME
       chmod - change file mode bits

SYNOPSIS
       chmod <mode> <file>...

DESCRIPTION
       Changes the permission bits of each FILE. MODE is either an
       octal number or a symbolic expression.

       Symbolic modes take the form [ugoa][+-=][rwx]. Omitting the who
       part means all. The execute bit matters: execve refuses to run a
       file that does not have it.

EXAMPLES
       chmod 644 notes.txt
       chmod +x script.csh
       chmod go-w /mnt/shared
       chmod u=rwx,go=rx /bin/tool

SEE ALSO
       chown(1), stat(1)
